menu "Angular linearization LUT"

    config ESP_ANGLE_LUT_FULL_SCALE_COUNTS
        int "Angle sensor counts per revolution"
        range 256 65536
        default 16384
        help
            Number of distinct native angle counts in one revolution. It must
            be a power of two and no smaller than the LUT bin count. Typical
            values are 4096 for a 12-bit sensor, 16384 for a 14-bit sensor and
            65536 for a 16-bit sensor.

    config ESP_ANGLE_LUT_BIN_COUNT
        int "Angular correction table bins"
        range 16 256
        default 256
        help
            Number of equally spaced bins over one revolution. The value must
            be a power of two that divides the configured sensor full scale.

    config ESP_ANGLE_LUT_MAX_ABS_CORRECTION_COUNTS
        int "Maximum accepted absolute correction (sensor counts)"
        range 1 32767
        default 1024
        help
            Reject uploaded tables containing a larger correction, expressed
            in native sensor counts. With the default 16384-count scale, 1024
            counts correspond to 22.5 degrees. Adjust this value when changing
            sensor resolution if the same angular limit is desired. At runtime
            the accepted limit is clamped below half a revolution.

endmenu
